  "about": "Controller Grant 1.2.0 adds app_asset, the app asset a machine is the back end of, so what a person said through that machine can show which app spoke. 1.1.0 keeps its identifier and is still honoured. Each case gives an attribute block and the version of the schema it is held to, and says whether the block is admitted. The schemas are the published files in contracts/asset-grants; the identifiers are the Blake3-256 digest of each with $id replaced by 44 '#'. Checked in Go by schemas/controller_grant_vectors_test.go and independently, from the published schema file alone, by contracts/check_controller_grant_vectors.py. A case marked value_fault is refused for the type or value of an attribute, which the schema file decides and the Go check of names does not.",
